{"name":"Rosa Chinensis","hex":"#c77579","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rosa","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["to hide, vanish, shadow"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["no-show, someone who does not show up as expected"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rosa"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rosa chinensis","blocks":[{"text":"Rosa chinensis, known commonly as the China rose, Chinese rose, or Bengal rose, is a member of the genus Rosa native to Southwest China in Guizhou, Hubei, and Sichuan Provinces. The first publication of Rosa chinensis was in 1768 by Nikolaus Joseph von Jacquin in Observationum Botanicarum, 3, p. 7 & plate 55."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Rosa_chinensis.jpg/330px-Rosa_chinensis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosa_chinensis","wikidata":"Q344900"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Rosa_chinensis0.jpg/500px-Rosa_chinensis0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Rosa_chinensis0.jpg/500px-Rosa_chinensis0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rosa chinensis 'Old Blush'","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARosa_chinensis0.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/%E7%99%BE%E8%8A%B1%E5%9C%96%E5%8D%B7-%E9%95%B7%E6%98%A5%E8%8A%B1.jpg/250px-%E7%99%BE%E8%8A%B1%E5%9C%96%E5%8D%B7-%E9%95%B7%E6%98%A5%E8%8A%B1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/%E7%99%BE%E8%8A%B1%E5%9C%96%E5%8D%B7-%E9%95%B7%E6%98%A5%E8%8A%B1.jpg/500px-%E7%99%BE%E8%8A%B1%E5%9C%96%E5%8D%B7-%E9%95%B7%E6%98%A5%E8%8A%B1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://t